From: Ferrite overlay
Subject: [PATCH] std.Target.Os.Tag: add `ferrite`

Add `.ferrite` to the OS tag enum so stdlib code (and any future Zig
fork built with Ferrite as a real target) can reference it in switches
the normal way. Stock nix-released Zig 0.16.0 still parses target
strings via the compiler binary, which doesn't know `.ferrite`, so
this enum entry stays dead code there — but adding it now keeps the
other patches honest about the discriminator and lets the fork at
midstall/zig build cleanly.

--- a/std/Target.zig
+++ b/std/Target.zig
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
         plan9,
         rtems,
         serenity,
+        ferrite,

         dragonfly,
         freebsd,
